 17592186332100 13194139535117 true] [17592186332096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332101 13194139535117 true] [17592186332096 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535117 true] [17592186332096 1041 "selection" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332096 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332101 13194139535117 true] [17592186332096 1110 #uuid "bee02561-94bc-51a3-92e1-ef402611f168" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332097 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332097 1111 #uuid "cf27b51b-1135-5277-a0d1-0bce6ca54618" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332098 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332098 1111 #uuid "4e502a6a-0a25-52b4-954b-5e4f41c2b638" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332099 1034 "III only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332099 1111 #uuid "372a4852-a0f8-5082-a868-97c444a1ce70" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332100 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332100 1111 #uuid "931f9b6b-fb51-5532-afae-cb69fe0718dc" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332101 1034 "II only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332101 1111 #uuid "10b09b93-ae6c-50eb-a181-680385b00433" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332103 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1089 "q-334148" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1100 "Which of the following equations is a Clairaut differential equation?\n\n- $y=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′}-1)^{4}$\n- $y{y}^{′}-x{y}^{5}-4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{2}$\n- $x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({y}^{′}+2)-y=0$" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1113 #uuid "322a6327-4647-5c0f-a844-3881dd52b8ef" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332102 1145 "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Clairaut differential equation of the form $y=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\ng({y}^{′})=({y}^{′}-1)^{4}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is *not* a Clairaut differential equation. Dividing the equation by $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-x{y}^{4}-4{x}^{3}{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)y.\n$$\n\nThis equation cannot be written in the form $y=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation III is a Clairaut differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({y}^{′}+2),\n$$\n\nwhich is a Clairaut differential equation of the form $y=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\ng({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡({y}^{′}+2).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332104 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332105 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332106 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332107 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332108 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1041 "selection" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332105 13194139535117 true] [17592186332103 1110 #uuid "1759dba0-2b4d-56e3-88f7-63158716ed62" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332104 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332104 1111 #uuid "69b0b65d-894c-5799-8351-3bcd6383f33b" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332105 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332105 1111 #uuid "2894756b-60dd-5e1f-b16c-6d93e3c681cd" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332106 1034 "I only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332106 1111 #uuid "8d3fcb83-dcff-5edf-9e76-a684d5f68dde" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332107 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332107 1111 #uuid "fcafc1f0-a79a-5c22-aa55-2bfec22bf162" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332108 1034 "II only" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535117 true] [17592186332108 1111 #uuid "547244de-598b-55fd-abcd-85754a87f3a2" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332110 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1089 "q-334205" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-({y}^{′})^{2}+4({y}^{′})^{3}.\n$$" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1113 #uuid "5610e9ad-4bbc-520f-a9ee-8f20106ec156" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332109 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-({y}^{′})^{2}+4({y}^{′})^{3},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp-{p}^{2}+4{p}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp-{p}^{2}+4{p}^{3})^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-2p{p}^{′}+12{p}^{2}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-2p+12{p}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp-{p}^{2}+4{p}^{3},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx-{c}^{2}+4{c}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332111 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332112 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332113 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332114 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332115 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1041 "selection" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332114 13194139535117 true] [17592186332110 1110 #uuid "ece273b9-a288-5f6e-883e-7299c985caf7" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332111 1034 "y={c}^{3}x-{c}^{2}+4{c}^{3}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332111 1111 #uuid "173418ee-ef16-52fc-9ff5-13da63479757" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332112 1034 "y=cx-{c}^{2}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332112 1111 #uuid "4a718216-2ede-55da-b7cf-5cdf145de7f9" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332113 1034 "y={c}^{2}x-{c}^{2}+4{c}^{3}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332113 1111 #uuid "36907a14-2e66-5a1a-b2c4-b938cb71f893" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332114 1034 "y=cx-{c}^{2}+4{c}^{3}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332114 1111 #uuid "d93a1f7a-4ffd-5147-b32f-2cdfc1594730" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332115 1034 "y=cx+4{c}^{3}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332115 1111 #uuid "309f7400-90e1-5837-9119-e5b571314189" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332117 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1089 "q-334209" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1100 "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+{e}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1113 #uuid "28d9a796-6415-5070-af00-f7842262a2dc" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332116 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+{e}^{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+{e}^{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+{e}^{p})^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+{e}^{p}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+{e}^{p})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+{e}^{p},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+{e}^{c}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332118 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332119 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332120 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332121 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332122 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1041 "selection" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332121 13194139535117 true] [17592186332117 1110 #uuid "6a857ee0-e13d-5cab-b59e-3f67306b436b" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332118 1034 "y=cx+{e}^{2c}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332118 1111 #uuid "918ba645-4d28-539c-8015-05ef51603b9e" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332119 1034 "y={c}^{3}x+{e}^{c}" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535117 true] [17592186332119 1111 #uuid "90828dbd-97ff-58fc-ac9e-ab44f434c958" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332120 1034 "y=cx+c" 13194139535117 true] [17592186332120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139